Subject: Competitive play: a set's game starts itself into its RANKED search
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

A competitive set starts in the launcher's lobby: once both players pressed
Ready to play!, both launchers start the game with the set handed over
(charged_configure_competitive_start in src/platform/competitive_match.cpp,
with the player's own Mii, which the launcher made from their Discord
account). Such a game goes through the retail online flow by itself, one
step at a time, as the player would:

- the title is passed at once, as by Skip intro, and the main menu chooses
  Online (SelectItem, with its own checks and the online save's load);
- the online Mii menu chooses the player's own Mii on its page (SelectMii),
  and its overlay presses Use, which selects the Mii, keeps its save slot and
  goes on to the WFC login;
- the login, once it succeeded and DWC ended the friend list sync that
  follows it (DWC refuses a search before), goes on into the RANKED search
  for one player, as the online menu's RANKED and the player count would
  (InitializeOnlineMatch, the matchmaking draft scene) instead of the online
  menu; the profile service's RANKED steering then lets the two games find
  only each other;
- the connection check accepts the set's opponent at once and rejects
  anybody else (who is then left out of the search, as retail does);
- every popup is answered with its first option; one that is not harmless
  (anything but a low battery, a Mii's first time online, a new online save)
  ends the set, and the retail flow behind it goes on;
- back from the online match, the series is over (the online menu still
  comes up, under the host closing the game).

The captain draft, the match and the series are retail, by the set's rules
(0046). A game without a set handed over, and so the main menu's own Online,
stays retail.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
index ef60b8a..e6e0802 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_competitive.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -34,6 +34,33 @@ bool mscharged_competitive_tweak(int tweak);
 // otherwise `stadium`.
 int mscharged_competitive_stadium(int stadium);
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// A set's game (the launcher's Ready to play!, tweak patch 0047): it starts
+// itself into the set's RANKED search, one step at a time. Each answer is
+// for this game's set only; without one everything stays retail.
+// The main menu, once ready: true to choose Online now (once).
+bool mscharged_competitive_take_main_menu(void);
+// The online Mii menu, once ready: the position of the set's Mii in its list
+// (`official_indices`, `count` of them) to choose now, or -1.
+int mscharged_competitive_mii_position(const int* official_indices, int count);
+// The Mii's overlay, once ready: true to press Use now (once).
+bool mscharged_competitive_take_use(void);
+// The login succeeded: true to go on into the RANKED search (once) instead
+// of the online menu.
+bool mscharged_competitive_take_ranked(void);
+// The login succeeded, before the RANKED step: true while the set's game
+// waits for DWC's friend list sync after the login (no search starts then).
+bool mscharged_competitive_ranked_waits(void);
+// The connection check with these two machines' WFC profiles: 0 accept (the
+// set's opponent), 1 reject (anybody else), -1 the player decides.
+int mscharged_competitive_connection(unsigned first, unsigned second);
+// A popup (ePopupMenu) ready for input: the option to press, or -1 for the
+// player's own choice. One that is not harmless ends the set.
+int mscharged_competitive_popup(int type);
+// The front end is back from an online match (the series is over).
+void mscharged_competitive_back_from_game(void);
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
